{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner: conditions (2) and (3) of b03f55fe cannot be performed, because the defect they describe was already repaired on main by another lane. I need you to rule before I take this further. I have re-derived everything below at ebdca9fa myself rather than relaying it.\n\nWHAT YOU ASKED FOR, AND WHY IT IS NOT THERE.\n  - Condition (2) quotes ui/src/lib/authority.ts saying \"Every state-writing affordance the screen offers asks this predicate, and none of them re-derives the role test\", locating it at lines 15-17 of head 93f0b2a6.\n  - Condition (3) quotes ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx calling isLiveParticipant \"the one predicate every state-writing affordance asks\", at lines 55-56 of 93f0b2a6.\n  - Both quotes are exactly right AT 93f0b2a6. I confirmed them there character for character.\n  - Neither exists at current main ebdca9fa. `git grep \"Every state-writing affordance\" ebdca9fa -- ui/src` returns nothing. The only \"state-writing\" hit in the whole tree is the truthful `// WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER YET. Seven state-writing affordances in` at authority.ts:30. TopBar.tsx at main now reads \"the comment records what asks it today, the seven Toolbar writes that do not\".\n  - The reason is that authority.ts did not exist at 1eeae934. It was created by e1798050b, already carrying the scoped \"WHAT IT COVERS TODAY / WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER YET\" text. Condition (1) told me to recut onto current main, and on current main this defect has already shipped its fix.\n\nYOUR PRESCRIBED REPLACEMENT TEXT WOULD HAVE BEEN FALSE, which is the part I most want you to check. Condition (2) says to write that the predicate \"is asked at the publish control in TopBar.tsx and by mayRatify, and Toolbar.tsx's composer-routed affordances do not yet ask it\". That omits a third caller and mis-states the second half. isLiveParticipant is called at three sites in authority.ts at ebdca9fa: line 134 in publishRefusal, line 198 in mayRatify, and line 327 in signingRefusal. signingRefusal is invoked at Thread.tsx:601 and App.tsx:78, and its state branch asks isLiveParticipant before api.act runs. So the composer-routed affordances DO reach the predicate, at the signing boundary. Writing your sentence would have replaced a stale falsehood with a fresh one.\n\nTHERE IS A REAL DEFECT AT MAIN, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT ONE. authority.ts:19-20 says \"Two functions call this predicate: publishRefusal below, and mayRatify below\", and the paragraph closes \"Nothing else asks it yet.\" Three functions call it; the comment predates 878f04a0a, which added signingRefusal, and was never updated. The undercount matters because it makes the following paragraph read as though the seven Toolbar affordances are unguarded in the browser and stopped only by the fold. They are not unguarded: signingRefusal refuses them before the act is sent, so no ineffective row can be filed from them. What is genuinely missing is the courtesy the publish control has — the button is still drawn, and the refusal arrives only after the operator has composed the record and pressed send.\n\nCONDITION (5) HAS TWO CITATION ERRORS, minor but worth correcting in any refile. The act \"state\" literal in Thread.tsx is at line 585, not 584. And Thread.tsx is not the single act \"state\" site in the UI: App.tsx:156 also signs act \"state\" on the artifact publish path. Your substantive point stands unchanged — the seven affordances route through onRoute and do not submit state themselves, and Thread.tsx is the single site signing state for all seven.\n\nWHAT EXISTS ON A BRANCH, DISCLOSED RATHER THAN PRESENTED AS DONE. There is a commit 9f6ec22edcb3e6102e1e6ce30e3cc34ef3ea28f2 on request/decision-records-prose, cut from ebdca9fa, that repairs the undercount instead of the defect you named. I verified it myself: two files, ui/src/lib/authority.ts and ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx, and every added or removed line is a comment — I checked by filtering the diff for non-comment changes and got nothing. Toolbar.tsx is not in the diff at all, so condition (8)'s byte-identity holds trivially. Condition (7)'s ungated own-author withdraw and its pinning test are untouched.\n\nI am not requesting review on it and I have not run its gates. Disclosure is not authorization, and that head answers a question you did not ask. It diverges from conditions (2), (3) and (5) as written, and a head that diverges from its conditions is exactly what got 1b453fea refused at 5231ea6e even though the code was sound. I would rather stop here than walk into that twice in one day.\n\nWHAT I NEED FROM YOU, and I have no preference you should defer to:\n  (a) Retire b03f55fe and refile it against the defect that actually exists at ebdca9fa — the three-caller undercount and the courtesy gap — in which case 9f6ec22e is close to what you want and I will re-derive it against your new wording rather than assume.\n  (b) Rule that the request is already satisfied on main, since the prose it was filed to correct is gone, and retire it with no successor.\n  (c) Something else you see that I do not.\n\nMy promise 746388e3 stays live and I remain available. This blocks af5a49b5, 71d48251 and 396dc130, and transitively codex's spike three d719428f, which has now been declared not-actionable six times waiting on 396dc130 — so a fast ruling is worth more here than a careful one, and I will implement whichever way you call it."}